WEBVTT

00:00:00.280 --> 00:00:03.050
Heat and flooding shape cold storage decisions.

00:00:03.080 --> 00:00:05.050
This is GEONOS.

00:00:05.080 --> 00:00:11.100
Compare two buildings, inspect the evidence, and plan your next site visit.

00:00:12.572 --> 00:00:20.112
Built during the hackathon, this NYC workspace brings six Meta models together with official public data.

00:00:21.572 --> 00:00:25.542
Search over a million outlines across five boroughs.

00:00:25.572 --> 00:00:30.872
Select 572 Smith, then 592.

00:00:30.932 --> 00:00:38.472
Explore layers and 3D, with building and whole-lot measurements clearly organized.

00:00:39.863 --> 00:00:44.203
Choose a measurement and test twenty thousand square feet.

00:00:44.263 --> 00:00:49.163
See each building’s result, then choose the next fact to verify.

00:00:50.655 --> 00:00:54.995
Explore modeled surface water around each building.

00:00:55.295 --> 00:01:05.795
Compare the current sea-level scenario with 2050, then focus on surrounding ground and drainage questions.

00:01:07.280 --> 00:01:14.180
Bring regional projections, station history and paired heat and moisture observations into the discussion.

00:01:14.640 --> 00:01:17.860
Use them to shape equipment and operating questions.

00:01:19.322 --> 00:01:23.052
Follow Lombardy’s parent and child energy reports.

00:01:23.082 --> 00:01:29.822
Trace each reported area and ask which meters and operating uses each report covers.

00:01:31.238 --> 00:01:35.258
Muse Voice turns spoken questions into editable text.

00:01:35.398 --> 00:01:41.578
Muse Spark connects your conversation to official records, tools and their source references.

00:01:42.988 --> 00:01:47.838
SAM 3.1 locates roof and tree image regions in dated aerials.

00:01:47.868 --> 00:01:54.048
Switch between sites, inspect overlays, and open the original images.

00:01:55.530 --> 00:02:01.740
Muse Wonder reviews structured summaries from both sites and suggests checks covering roofs, equipment, tree

00:02:01.770 --> 00:02:04.590
context and the map and image.

00:02:06.072 --> 00:02:10.252
DINOv2 highlights imagery windows for closer inspection.

00:02:10.472 --> 00:02:17.212
Compare the 2020 and 2024 aerials in your browser and prepare a site-visit question.

00:02:18.697 --> 00:02:26.957
Muse Image illustrates the inspection plan: what we know, what to verify, and what could change.

00:02:28.363 --> 00:02:31.103
Open sources and record dates.

00:02:31.483 --> 00:02:39.103
Export the comparison and your conditions, ready for a conversation with the owner or project team.

00:02:40.572 --> 00:02:42.862
Request roof plans and meter schedules.

00:02:42.892 --> 00:02:45.792
Verify usable space and power.

00:02:45.932 --> 00:02:51.072
Then visit the site to inspect entrances, drainage and equipment elevations.
